      "date": "2025-11-11T11:27:42.000Z",
      "title": "Second quarter 2026 earnings: EPS in line with expectations, revenues disappoint",
      "body": "Second quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹21.35 (up from ₹17.59 in 2Q 2025). Revenue: ₹660.6b (up 14% from 2Q 2025). Net income: ₹47.4b (up 21% from 2Q 2025). Profit margin: 7.2% (up from 6.7% in 2Q 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue missed analyst estimates by 1.2%. Earnings per share (EPS) were mostly in line with analyst estimates. Revenue is forecast to grow 5.0% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 11% growth forecast for the Metals and Mining industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 18% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 20% per year.",
